From 5a5f2cc76c1e7d45b1654514291d5645865cba9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 15:54:56 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kernel): populate session_id/worktree_id/expires_at on
 claim leases (d71a824b)

The claim write path left session_id, worktree_id, and expires_at null on
every lease, so the dashboard's live session/worktree/liveness badges (PR #357)
had nothing real to render.

Wire the three fields end-to-end:
- worktree_id: resolved at the CLI boundary (lib/forge-issues.js) from
  FORGE_WORKTREE_ID or the current worktree dir name (detectWorktree), threaded
  as context.worktreeId for the claim op only (worktree detection shells to git).
- session_id: already flowed from FORGE_SESSION_ID; confirmed + covered by tests.
- expires_at: new DEFAULT_LEASE_TTL_MS (8h) in lease-enforcer; the boundary passes
  context.leaseTtlMs, the claim event carries lease_ttl_ms, and buildClaimRow
  derives expires_at = claimed_at + ttl when no explicit --expires. FORGE_LEASE_TTL_MS
  overrides; 0/invalid opts out to a null (never-expiring) lease.

Broker-direct callers (and all existing null-default tests) carry no ttl, so the
historical null=never-expires default is byte-identical for them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
